{
  "$comment": "EXP-1560 (was A-16): THE Devices page, one spec ×4 (web my-machines.tsx + device-logins.tsx, desktop machines.rs, iOS AgentsView + DeviceLogins, Android AgentsScreen). LAYOUT: each section (`mine` with its `+ Add device` pill, `team`) is a GRID of device CARDS: columns = max(1, floor((width + card.gap) / (card.minWidth + card.gap))) over the section's content width, gap `card.gap` both ways (a phone in portrait gets 1 column, a phone in landscape or a tablet 2 or more). Groups: online cards first in the list's own order, then the muted `offline` label spanning the grid, then every offline card in its own grid, dimmed (opacity 0.6). CARD = THE GlassCard surface (fill + hairline + radius), padding `card.padding`, two rows. TOP row: left a column of [name (truncates) + `v{version}` beside it (warning tone when the caller's own device is outdated, else muted) + the default star] over [the status line (Online dot / Last seen …) + the `This device` / `Shared` tags]; right the `⋯` overflow (a ghost icon button, `copy.deviceActions`) opening THE Menu. Menu items, in order: the update line (when the device has an `update` / `update_queued` attention item: its `text` as a disabled muted row), `Update` (only when that item's action is `update`; busy while requested), `copy.settings` (own REGISTERED devices; opens the Device settings dialog). A team device's menu holds only a team owner's `copy.removeFromTeam`; a card with no item draws no `⋯` (its slot stays empty). BOTTOM row: the logins as ICONS ONLY, in `sortDeviceLogins` order: each a ghost icon button (`card.iconSize` square) holding the agent's brand mark (`card.markSize`), THE run-mark badge (AgentRunMark `needs_input`: amber dot top-right, ringed in the card's ground) ON every login that has a `login` attention item. With more than `card.maxAccountIcons` logins only the first maxAccountIcons-1 show, then a ghost `⋯` (`copy.moreAccounts`) that reveals the rest in place (`accountIcons`). Own, online cards with an agent to add end the row with a ghost `+` (`copy.addAccount`). A device that reported accounts but holds NO login says `noAccount` muted in the row; one that never reported says `checking`. EXP-1600 KEEP SIGNED IN: a claude sign-in is the long-lived `claude setup-token` login BY DEFAULT on every client (Add account, Sign in, the menu, the MCP `account_login`): the same link + code-paste dialog, the machine keeps the one-year token (`tokenExpiresAt`). The dialog says the trade-off in ONE muted line under its status line (`copy.keepSignedInNote`) and offers the refresh-grant browser login only as a ghost text button (`copy.useBrowserLogin`, re-queues the SAME target with longLived false; from there `copy.useKeepSignedIn` goes back). Codex has no setup-token: its dialog has neither line nor button. A device that refuses an Add with `copy.longLivedRefused` is an older build: the dialog re-queues ONCE as the browser login. ACCOUNT PREVIEW: hovering an icon (pointer) opens THE hover card; a click (pointer) or a tap (touch) opens THE account menu (AccountChipMenu, in order: `Sign in` when signed out or needs_relogin (claude = Keep signed in); claude only and only when it does NOT sign in: `copy.switchToKeepSignedIn` without a token, `copy.renewKeepSignedIn` with one; `Sign out` when signed in; `Remove account` always; a team device's icon only previews, a tap opens the preview card). Both lead with the SAME header: the email (else the label) on top, the plan muted under it, the login's `status` line in warning tone when it has an attention item, then the usage windows (UsageWindows `full` density: title + reset, then meter + percent: the 5h session, the weeks, the per-model windows, each with its reset). The hover card ends with a pill for the item's action: `sign_in` = `copy.signIn`, `keep_signed_in` = `copy.switchToKeepSignedIn` (status `switch`) or `copy.renewKeepSignedIn` (status `renew`); both keep_signed_in pills open the long-lived sign-in for that profile. ATTENTION (pure, `deviceListRow`): items in order: every login whose health is needs_relogin, then every signed_out login, then every OTHER login with `limitHit` (a fresh usage window at ≥ 100%; text `limitReached`, never an action), then (own devices only, EXP-1600) every OTHER claude login whose `tokenExpiresAt` is within `keepSignedIn.renewWithinDays` days of `now` or past it (text `renewSoon`, status `renew`, the yearly reminder), then every OTHER claude login with NO `tokenExpiresAt` (text `switchPrompt`, status `switch`: the one-tap prompt for logins made before the default changed), both with action `keep_signed_in` only on the caller's own online device, then the update line. A login yields at most one item. An AGENT with no login at all (a CLI installed, never signed in: `profiles` empty or absent) is NOT an item and badges nothing: the old IDE bug where mint read `Signed out` because Codex was installed. The update line exists only on the caller's own device: `updateQueued` when an update is parked behind live sessions (no action), else `updateAvailable` (with `latest`) when the client's own version compare says `outdated` (action `update` only for a SERVER — the CLI daemon is the one device that acts on an update request; a desktop app updates itself — and only while it is online and registered). Login actions (`sign_in`, never on a limit item) only on the caller's own online device. Team devices: read-only (no `+`, no actions), a team owner's Remove in the `⋯`.",
